{
 "_doc": "The Chicago River at the forks AS THE THOMPSON 1830 PLAT DRAWS IT, committed BESIDE the Wright 1834 planform in data/terrain/epochs/e1834_harbor_cut/river.geojson and NOT over it. Neither line is silently preferred: the Wright trace remains the planform of record and nothing in the scene is derived from this file. T-0685 (piece 2 of T-0453), on the owner's reading that the Thompson plat says something different at Wolf Point. It does -- see docs/RESEARCH/thompson_forks_georeference.md for the measurement, and the ticket for the ruling it is waiting on.",
 "source": "thompson_plat_1830",
 "georeference": "data/traces/gcp/thompson_1830_gcps.json (similarity fit, RMS 4.9 m over 22 street-corridor crossings against modern OSM control)",
 "read_on": "2026-09-05",
 "method": "The two bank lines are the two largest 8-connected components of the sheet's ink in a window over the forks, at an ink threshold of 40 grey levels below the local paper. No pixel of either line was placed by hand. The North Division shore is sampled as the westmost ink per raster row down the branch and the southmost ink per raster column along the stem; the West Division shore is a single stroke and is sampled as the mean ink column per row. Sampled every 5 px and thinned to a 9 px (4.7 m) minimum spacing.",
 "confidence": "inferred",
 "confidence_note": "The POSITION of each vertex is a measurement, to about +/- 3 m (2.6 m of georeference picking plus a pixel of line width). What is graded `inferred` rather than `documented` is the identification: that the ink line Thompson's copyist drew is the bank of the river at a stated date. The sheet is a plat of lots, its river is drawn freehand -- the stroke visibly wavers where a surveyed line would not -- and the surviving artifact is a Canal Commissioners' working copy dated to at least 1836. It bounds the blocks; it was not the object of the survey.",
 "may_not": "Be used to move any waterline, bank, heightfield, wharf, landing or lot in this project. data/sources/thompson_plat_1830.json's standing instruction -- read the plat for its stated figures, never trace it for geometry -- is unchanged; this file exists so that the disagreement can be MEASURED, which T-0453 asked for and which no committed artifact could answer before.",
